      'Tenerife has quietly become one of the best stag do destinations in Europe — and once you look at the maths, it is obvious why. Cheap flights from almost every UK and Irish airport, guaranteed sunshine all year round, a beachfront strip built for going out, and enough activities to fill a whole weekend without anyone getting bored. If you are the best man staring at a group chat of twelve lads waiting for a plan, this guide is for you.',
      'The golden rule of a good stag weekend is simple: it cannot just be bars. Two nights of drinking with no structure is how groups fall apart, arguments start, and the stag ends up face-down by 9pm on the first night. What holds a stag do together is a proper daytime activity — something competitive, a bit ridiculous, and impossible to do at home. That is the anchor everything else is built around.',
      'The number one group activity for stags in Tenerife right now is a self-guided <a href="/en/escape-game">outdoor escape game</a>. Split the crew into teams, each with a phone, and race around a real town cracking clues and solving the mystery. There is no fixed time — you play any day, at your own pace — and something competitive kicks in the moment the first puzzle falls. It gets everyone involved, not just the loud ones, and it is the story everyone tells on the flight home.',
      'The escape game works for any group size — you simply book one phone per team and set them all off together, then meet for a drink to compare times and crown the winners. See the group options on our <a href="/en/stag-hen-party-tenerife">stag & hen party page</a>, and the rest of the island\'s experiences on our <a href="/en/activities">things to do in Tenerife</a> page. One plan, the whole crew sorted.',
      'For the second day, this is where you add the water and adrenaline. Tenerife is stacked with group experiences — jet ski sessions, boat parties, catamaran cruises with a bar on board, parasailing over the coast. You can see the full line-up on our <a href="/en/activities">things to do in Tenerife</a> page. A morning boat trip followed by an afternoon on the beach is the perfect recovery day between two big nights.',
      'On nightlife: Playa Las Americas is the engine room. The Veronicas strip and the surrounding bars are wall-to-wall stag and hen groups, so your crew will feel right at home. Costa Adeje next door is a slightly classier option if you want cocktail bars over shot bars. The key is to eat properly before you go out — a big group that skips dinner never makes it past midnight.',
      'A few planning tips from experience. Book your water activities before you fly — weekends and peak season fill up fast. Sort a group airport transfer in advance. Put one person (not the stag) in charge of the money. And make the daytime feel like a proper send-off — matching tees, a custom forfeit for the slowest escape-game team, and a toast when the winners finish.',
